---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import SourceList from '../../../components/SourceList.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../../components/RelatedGuides.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import AdsterraBanner300x250 from '../../../components/AdsterraBanner300x250.astro';
import { sourceUrls } from '../../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Beginner Guide — First-Session Prep & Common Mistakes';
const description = 'Prepare for your first DragonSword Awakening session: check installation needs, avoid unsupported upgrade priorities, and understand what the co-op label means.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/guides/beginner/';
const article = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-10-20', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' } };
const sources = [{ label: 'Official Steam store page', href: sourceUrls.steam, note: 'Reviewed October 19, 2026: supports the SSD/storage requirements, language support, single-player and Online Co-op labels, Cooking and Familiars. It does not specify an optimal starting route or spending order.' }];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/beginner/' }, { label: 'Beginner Guide' }]} /><article><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Guide · Getting started</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Beginner Guide</h1><p>Guide updated October 20, 2026</p></header>
    <QuickAnswer title="Check your setup before planning your first session."><p>Confirm the installation drive is an SSD, check the PC requirements, and choose a supported text language. Treat Cooking, Familiars and co-op as systems to understand when you encounter them—not a mandatory first-session spending list.</p></QuickAnswer>
    <div class="article-body"><SectionHeader title="Before you start" description="Installation and reading checks you can finish before entering Orbis." /><ul class="checklist"><li><strong>Installation drive:</strong> check the drive where the game will actually be installed. Steam requires an SSD for an optimal experience; having an SSD elsewhere in the PC does not satisfy that installation advice.</li><li><strong>Available space:</strong> Steam lists 25 GB. Check the selected drive's free space and the installer's displayed requirement before proceeding.</li><li><strong>PC specifications:</strong> compare your machine with the <a href="/system-requirements/">minimum and recommended requirements</a>. A matching specification is not a tested frame-rate promise.</li><li><strong>Text language:</strong> Steam lists English interface and subtitles, with full audio listed for Korean. Choose text you can comfortably read for skill and item descriptions; English text support does not mean English voice acting.</li></ul>
      <figure class="guide-visual"><img src="/media/beginner/install-on-ssd.svg" width="480" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A game folder points to the SSD: check that this drive is the installation destination." /><figcaption>Installation sketch: the requirement applies to the drive holding the game. Editorial illustration based on the Steam SSD note; not an installer screenshot.</figcaption></figure>
      <h2>Long loads or missing textures? Check the installation first</h2><p>The developer warns that an HDD installation may cause long loading times, texture pop-in, frame-rate drops or crashes. If those symptoms occur, checking the installation drive is a useful first check. They do not prove the drive is the only cause, and this guide does not promise that moving the game will fix every performance issue.</p>
      <h2>Before spending materials, identify what the action buys</h2><p><strong>Our suggestion:</strong> before confirming an unfamiliar upgrade or craft, read the displayed cost and effect. Identify which item or character receives the result and whether that result addresses a problem you have now. If the information is missing or unclear, postpone that optional action until you can explain what you are paying for.</p><figure class="guide-visual"><img src="/media/beginner/before-spending.svg" width="480" height="540" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Before an optional spend, check the cost, effect and current need. Pause if any is unclear." /><figcaption>Use this reading aid before an optional upgrade or craft. Editorial illustration, not a game menu or a recommended upgrade sequence.</figcaption></figure><p>This is a reading habit, not a tested resource strategy. It does not establish that a material is rare, an upgrade is reversible, or one Hero should receive all early investment. We do not prescribe a first awakening, material reserve or spending order here.</p>
      <AdsterraNativeBanner />
      <h2>Cooking and Familiars are not an automatic priority list</h2><p>The official description confirms ingredient-based Cooking and collectible Familiars that accompany you. It does not establish which recipe or Familiar a beginner should obtain first.</p><p><strong>Our suggestion:</strong> when either system becomes available to you, read its own instructions and any displayed requirements before using resources. Having ingredients alone is not a reason to craft every available dish. A Familiar appearing in promotional material is not evidence that you need it for your next task. This page does not supply unlock timings, recipe effects or a ranked shopping list.</p>
      <h2>Planning to start with a friend?</h2><p>Steam lists both Single-player and Online Co-op. The co-op label alone does not tell you which story sections, exploration areas or progression can be shared. Before planning a full playthrough together, check the <a href="/multiplayer/">confirmed co-op activities and remaining limitations</a>. Do not assume a whole-world shared campaign from the store label.</p>
      <AdsterraBanner300x250 />
      <h2>Choose the guide for the problem in front of you</h2><p>Once your setup is ready, use these specific next steps. They are separate tasks, not a required order of progression.</p><ul><li><strong>A skill prompt is missing:</strong> the <a href="/guides/combat-system/">Signal Skills troubleshooting guide</a> checks activation conditions.</li><li><strong>You want to check a connection between Heroes:</strong> <a href="/teams/">Team Planning</a> helps record a directional handoff without assuming a complete rotation.</li><li><strong>You want to compare a setup change:</strong> <a href="/builds/">Build Planning</a> helps keep the comparison conditions consistent.</li><li><strong>You are looking for a location:</strong> use the <a href="/map/">interactive map</a> and its published location coverage.</li></ul>
    </div><SourceList sources={sources} intro="The official listing supports the installation and feature facts above. Paragraphs marked ‘Our suggestion’ are editorial advice, not developer instructions or a tested opening walkthrough." /><RelatedGuides links={[{ label: 'PC Requirements', href: '/system-requirements/' }, { label: 'Multiplayer', href: '/multiplayer/' }]} /></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-wrap { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; } .article-header { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; } .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-light); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; } h1, h2 { line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.04em; } h1 { max-width: 760px; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem); margin: 0 0 0.7rem; } h2 { font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem); margin: 2.8rem 0 0.75rem; } .article-body { max-width: 760px; } .article-body p, li { color: var(--muted-strong); } .checklist { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.65rem 2rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; } li { padding-left: 0.25rem; } @media (max-width: 650px) { .checklist { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .guide-visual { max-width: 480px; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .guide-visual img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; }
  .guide-visual figcaption { margin-top: .65rem; color: var(--muted-strong); font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
